{"title":"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three distinct segments are chosen at random among the segments whose end-points are the vertices of a regular 12-gon. What is the probability that the lengths of these three segments are the three side lengths of a triangle with positive area?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917ac7b4c4abfb5dcbfeb67a98d1c7750a98a332.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ \\frac{553}{715} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\ \\frac{443}{572} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\ \\frac{111}{143} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)} \\ \\frac{81}{104} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\ \\frac{223}{286}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"462\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the answer. We calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fdd66831cbbb8238ab62234975610d1682bbb03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Assume that the circumradius of the 12-gon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the 6 different lengths are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087594ea26fa196b8e61bc20a36228270dc695f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34ace040475607683853fcfd4960a8f7fa6678c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, in increasing order. Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2db751b2ae00207df0235b8910c57863c37539d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = 2\\sin ( \\frac{k\\pi}{12} )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282347bc076812f54025bb07a70a9b7629637a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=(\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2})/2 \\approx 0.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"21\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7c4c84cd04bf09b23af76a4714f60d649e3e1e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04b3c77b28127f102faa7d02a8d482250455ab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=\\sqrt{2}\\approx 1.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c2269fb6c38a8a91f2e4e154428ef26b5c67f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=\\sqrt{3}\\approx 1.7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"22\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577b6797d0336b088c616bc231abdb417637fbaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5=(\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2})/2 = a_1 + a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"227\" height=\"24\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f6fbc2e7626aeb56f0ce68dc4bc69108b5fc35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Now, Consider the following inequalities:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b71690229e3b7c3449280bd248f4e069f42bfdd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3&gt;2a_1 &gt; a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f97caf3509f99c3ee8a68e890bccb4627df6996f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4&gt; a_1 + a_2&gt;a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27f146d38a744038c987b7216fde8f1f84c2039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4&lt;a_1 + a_3=a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751c212fdb5c388da472ec2cdae8b2c867ea0caa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_4 &gt; a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/56785739f1e0924f0447f0c4a534175f64ba7fda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a_2 = 2 = a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />. Thus any two segments with at least one them longer than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> have a sum greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34ace040475607683853fcfd4960a8f7fa6678c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, all triples (in increasing order) that can't be the side lengths of a triangle are the following. Note that x-y-z means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d6007536a8100d586122f9293e497270437d8177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_x, a_y, a_z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />:\n</p>\n<pre>1-1-3, 1-1-4, 1-1-5, 1-1-6,\n1-2-4, 1-2-5, 1-2-6,\n1-3-5, 1-3-6,\n2-2-6\n</pre>\n<p>Note that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> segments of each length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087594ea26fa196b8e61bc20a36228270dc695f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5d34d49a7eb6afd4874d7bdaf23946dbf63cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, respectively, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> segments of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34ace040475607683853fcfd4960a8f7fa6678c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> segments in total.\n</p><p>In the above list there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triples of the type a-a-b without <i>6</i>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triples of a-a-6 where a is not <i>6</i>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triples of a-b-c without <i>6</i>, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triples of a-b-6 where a, b are not <i>6</i>. So,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/664789c0327055b6f37b531076cf626d92f7dda1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1-p = \\frac{1}{66\\cdot 65\\cdot 64} ( 3\\cdot 3 \\cdot 12\\cdot 11\\cdot 12 + 2\\cdot 3 \\cdot 12\\cdot 11\\cdot 6 + 3\\cdot 6\\cdot 12^3 + 2\\cdot 6 \\cdot 12^2 \\cdot 6)\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a8e9ca2efa46c7a5930b5d482527ad3449f372c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{1}{66\\cdot 65\\cdot 64} (12^2 (99+33) + 12^3(18+6)) = \\frac{1}{66\\cdot 65\\cdot 64} (12^3 \\cdot 35) = \\frac{63}{286}\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c76874eb6e23bf26e7b1c6a81c8eb2dea47ee465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 223/286$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2013amc12a/364\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2013amc12a/364</a>\n</p><p>~dolphin7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A\">2013 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017231743\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 287/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7232/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.658      1 -total\n 58.93%    7.459      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.70%    4.898      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11750:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017231743 and revision id 180493. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}